<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001003"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001028"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Graus 2016 lists ADEM among autoimmune encephalitis syndromes. It is also an inflammatory demyelinating disease (sibling of MS, NMO, MOGAD).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001004"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Kawasaki disease is a medium-vessel vasculitis (Chapel Hill 2012).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001013"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001028"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>CASPR2 encephalitis is a neuronal-surface-antibody autoimmune encephalitis (limbic, Morvan or neuromyotonia phenotypes).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001014"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Chapel Hill 2012 lists anti-GBM disease as an immune-complex small-vessel vasculitis (glomerular and alveolar capillaritis); nephrologists often treat it as a glomerulonephritis instead.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001016"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001079"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Clinically amyopathic, anti-MDA5-positive disease is a dermatomyositis subtype.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001016"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="c_0001016_0001116"/>
    <relation>component_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>The label combines amyopathic dermatomyositis with rapidly progressive ILD.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="c_0001016_0001116">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.aurint.org/ontologies/ari-disease-proposed-hierarchy#hasComponent"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001116"/>
</owl:Restriction>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001017"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>ANCA-associated vasculitis is the pauci-immune small-vessel group (Chapel Hill 2012).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001017"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001140"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Chapel Hill defines AAV as necrotizing vasculitis with few or no immune deposits.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001019"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001139"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Antisynthetase syndrome is an inflammatory myopathy subgroup defined by anti-aminoacyl-tRNA-synthetase antibodies.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001019"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="c_0001019_0001139"/>
    <relation>component_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Antisynthetase syndrome is myositis, ILD, arthritis, Raynaud's and mechanic's hands with antisynthetase antibodies.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="c_0001019_0001139">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.aurint.org/ontologies/ari-disease-proposed-hierarchy#hasComponent"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001139"/>
</owl:Restriction>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001019"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="c_0001019_0001116"/>
    <relation>component_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Interstitial lung disease is a core feature, often the presenting one.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="c_0001019_0001116">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.aurint.org/ontologies/ari-disease-proposed-hierarchy#hasComponent"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001116"/>
</owl:Restriction>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001023"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001050"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>The 'and/or' entry is the union of autoimmune urticaria and autoimmune angioedema.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001025"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001035"/>
    <relation>manifestation_of</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Autoimmune central diabetes insipidus comes from lymphocytic infundibuloneurohypophysitis, the posterior-pituitary form of autoimmune hypophysitis. Do not group it with type 1 diabetes because of the name: it is a vasopressin disorder, not diabetes mellitus.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001029"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001028"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Anti-NMDAR encephalitis is the prototypical antibody-mediated autoimmune encephalitis.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001037"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001028"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Autoimmune limbic encephalitis is the limbic presentation of autoimmune encephalitis (Graus 2016).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001037"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001121"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Limbic encephalitis covers infectious and paraneoplastic causes; the autoimmune form is its immune-mediated subset. 0001121's definition reads only 'Anti-DPPX encephalitis' and needs fixing.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001039"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001139"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Immune-mediated necrotizing myopathy is an idiopathic inflammatory myopathy subgroup (ENMC 2017).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001043"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001109"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Type 1 autoimmune pancreatitis is the pancreatic form of IgG4-related disease; type 2 (idiopathic duct-centric) is not IgG4-related.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001045"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001116"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>low</confidence>
    <reason>PAP is a diffuse parenchymal lung disease listed with ILDs, but the alveoli fill with surfactant instead of interstitial inflammation or fibrosis.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001046"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Retinal vasculitis is a single-organ vasculitis.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001046"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001208"/>
