    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Parry-Romberg overlaps with linear morphea 'en coup de sabre' and is grouped with linear morphea in the Padua classification of juvenile localized scleroderma.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001172"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001171"/>
    <relation>manifestation_of</relation>
    <confidence>medium</confidence>
    <reason>Psoriatic arthritis is the joint arm of psoriatic disease (about 30% of people with psoriasis develop it), though arthritis comes before skin disease in about 15%.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001173"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
