    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>low</confidence>
    <reason>Susac syndrome is an autoimmune endotheliopathy of brain, retina and cochlea. It is often grouped with the vasculitides but is not in Chapel Hill 2012.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001180"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="c_0001180_0001027"/>
    <relation>component_of</relation>
    <confidence>low</confidence>
    <reason>Susac triad: encephalopathy, branch retinal artery occlusions, hearing loss. The hearing loss is microvascular, not classic autoimmune inner-ear disease.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

