<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001181"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001182"/>
    <relation>manifestation_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Sydenham chorea is a major Jones criterion of rheumatic fever.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001183"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001185"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Rheumatoid aortitis is rheumatoid vasculitis of the aorta.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001185"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Chapel Hill 2012 category 'vasculitis associated with systemic disease'.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001185"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001184"/>
    <relation>manifestation_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Vasculitis occurring in long-standing seropositive RA.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001190"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001196"/>
    <relation>manifestation_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Lupus nephritis is the renal manifestation of SLE.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001192"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001028"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>SREAT (Hashimoto's encephalopathy) is a steroid-responsive autoimmune encephalopathy; the Graus 2016 autoimmune encephalitis criteria include it.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001195"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001208"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Sympathetic ophthalmia is a bilateral granulomatous panuveitis.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001199"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001198"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Limited cutaneous SSc is one of the two main SSc subsets (LeRoy).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001199"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="c_0001199_0001176"/>
    <relation>component_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Raynaud's is the R in CREST. The other four features (calcinosis, esophageal dysmotility, sclerodactyly, telangiectasia) are not listed diseases.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="c_0001199_0001176">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.aurint.org/ontologies/ari-disease-proposed-hierarchy#hasComponent"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001176"/>
</owl:Restriction>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001200"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Large-vessel vasculitis (Chapel Hill 2012).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001201"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Giant cell arteritis is a large-vessel vasculitis (Chapel Hill 2012).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001202"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001079"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Anti-TIF1-gamma marks a dermatomyositis antibody subgroup (cancer-associated in adults).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001205"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001112"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Ulcerative colitis is one of the two main IBDs.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001207"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Hypocomplementemic urticarial vasculitis is an immune-complex small-vessel vasculitis (Chapel Hill 2012).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001210"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001208"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>VKH is a bilateral granulomatous panuveitis with extraocular melanocyte involvement.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001211"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001032"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Warm (IgG) AIHA is the commonest form of AIHA.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001213"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001013"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Morvan syndrome is the CASPR2-antibody phenotype with neuromyotonia plus encephalopathy.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001213"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="c_0001213_0001144"/>
    <relation>component_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Morvan syndrome is neuromyotonia plus encephalopathy (insomnia) plus dysautonomia, usually with CASPR2 antibodies.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="c_0001213_0001144">
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.aurint.org/ontologies/ari-disease-proposed-hierarchy#hasComponent"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001144"/>
</owl:Restriction>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001214"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001080"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>LADA is slowly progressive, GAD-antibody-positive autoimmune diabetes; the ADA classifies it as a form of type 1 diabetes.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001215"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001080"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Fulminant type 1 diabetes is a type 1 subtype (Japan Diabetes Society) with abrupt, near-total beta-cell destruction.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001216"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001048"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Hashimoto's is the chronic lymphocytic form of autoimmune thyroiditis. Note 0001048's own definition already describes the Hashimoto course, so the two are near-duplicates.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001217"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001037"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>AMPAR encephalitis usually presents as limbic encephalitis (Graus 2016).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001218"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001037"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>GABA-B receptor encephalitis usually presents as limbic encephalitis with seizures (Graus 2016).</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001219"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001051"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>low</confidence>
    <reason>Chapel Hill 2012 lists isolated aortitis as a single-organ vasculitis. The label says 'non-vasculitic' (probably meaning 'not part of systemic vasculitis'), so settle the label first.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001221"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001030"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>low</confidence>
    <reason>Autoimmune autonomic ganglionopathy (gAChR antibodies) often causes GI dysmotility, and AGID can be its limited form, but not all AGID is ganglionic-antibody mediated.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001222"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001028"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>GFAP astrocytopathy presents as meningoencephalomyelitis and is classed with the autoimmune encephalitides.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001223"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001002"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>An acquired inhibitor against factor IX is acquired hemophilia (0001002 carries ICD-10 D68.311, acquired hemophilia). Acquired hemophilia A is the common form, B the rare one.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001224"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001063"/>
    <relation>is_a</relation>
    <confidence>low</confidence>
    <reason>Nodopathies used to be CIDP subtypes; EAN/PNS 2021 split them off, so siblings is current practice.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

<owl:Axiom>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001225"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="https://diseases.autoimmuneregistry.org/disease/ARI_0001224"/>
    <relation>duplicate_of</relation>
    <confidence>high</confidence>
    <reason>Both describe neuropathy with nodal or paranodal antibodies (NF155, CNTN1, Caspr1); merge.</reason>
</owl:Axiom>

</rdf:RDF>
